B.a0X=new A.cd("Photosensitive epilepsy","Reflex epilepsy","Seizures triggered by flickering light or high-contrast patterns (strobe lights, screens, video games).",B.Ry,"Photoparoxysmal response to intermittent photic stimulation.","Covering one eye when exposed to flicker sharply reduces the photoparoxysmal response; blue-tinted (Z1) lenses also help.",!1)
B.Sk=s(["Perioral/jaw myoclonus while reading","May generalize if the trigger is not stopped","Usually a benign, genetically determined reflex epilepsy"],t.s)
B.a17=new A.cd("Reading epilepsy","Reflex epilepsy","Jaw or perioral myoclonus triggered specifically by reading, especially aloud, which can progress to a generalized seizure if reading continues.",B.Sk,"Focal (perisylvian/language network) discharges triggered by reading.",null,!1)
B.Sd=s(["Trigger is highly individual-specific music","Usually temporal lobe (often right-sided) semiology","Very rare"],t.s)
B.a1g=new A.cd("Musicogenic epilepsy","Reflex epilepsy","A rare reflex epilepsy in which specific music triggers a seizure, typically of temporal lobe onset.",B.Sd,"Temporal discharges elicited during the triggering stimulus.",null,!1)
B.Tj=s(["Triggered specifically by hot water exposure, especially over the head","Often focal seizures with impaired awareness"],t.s)
B.a10=new A.cd("Hot water epilepsy","Reflex epilepsy","Seizures triggered by contact with hot water, classically while bathing; more prevalent in some geographic populations.",B.Tj,"Focal temporal discharge.",null,!1)
B.S6=s(["Triggered by an unexpected startle","Often associated with an underlying structural brain abnormality or perinatal injury","Asymmetric tonic posturing is typical"],t.s)
B.a0Y=new A.cd("Startle epilepsy","Reflex epilepsy","Seizures triggered by a sudden, unexpected stimulus (loud noise, tap), typically producing an asymmetric tonic seizure.",B.S6,"Rapid generalized or bilateral discharge time-locked to the startle stimulus.",null,!1)
B.Rt=s(["Onset typically 3-12 months of age","Clustered brief spasms (flexion, extension, or mixed)","Developmental regression is a red flag","Requires urgent evaluation; first-line is hormonal therapy (ACTH or high-dose prednisolone) or vigabatrin (first choice in tuberous sclerosis)"],t.s)
B.a18=new A.cd("Infantile epileptic spasms syndrome (West syndrome)","Epilepsy syndrome","Clusters of brief flexor, extensor, or mixed spasms in infancy, part of West syndrome (spasms, hypsarrhythmia, developmental regression).",B.Rt,"Hypsarrhythmia: chaotic, high-amplitude slow activity with multifocal spikes.","Infantile spasms are a pediatric neurologic emergency \u2014 early treatment improves developmental outcome.",!1)
