B.SZ=s(["Onset under 1 year, often triggered by fever or heat","Prolonged, often hemiclonic seizures progressing to multiple seizure types","Developmental regression/plateau typically emerges in the second year","High risk of status epilepticus and SUDEP"],t.s)
B.a11=new A.cd("Dravet syndrome","Rare / genetic syndrome","Severe myoclonic epilepsy of infancy, usually caused by an SCN1A sodium-channel mutation, beginning with prolonged febrile/hemiclonic seizures in the first year of life.",B.SZ,"Often normal early, later generalized and multifocal spike-wave activity; photosensitivity is common.","A first prolonged febrile seizure before 12 months, especially hemiclonic or heat-triggered, should prompt SCN1A genetic testing for Dravet syndrome.",!0)
B.R1=s(['Triad: tonic, atonic ("drop") and atypical absence seizures',"Usual onset age 3-5 years","Intellectual disability/developmental regression is common","Often refractory to standard anti-seizure medications"],t.s)
